# Python cache files
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Local copies of repo-root templates — copy from the .example versions
# and fill in your own values. Templates stay tracked, locals do not.
/.env
/config.py

# Deprecated tools
depr/

# Example sandbox directories
examples/advanced/**/sandbox_notebook/
examples/advanced/**/demo_sandbox/

# Sandboxes written by running the demos (create_new_sandbox numbers them).
# Digit-suffixed on purpose: examples/*/transcripts/sandbox/ is the committed
# output of the worked examples and must stay tracked.
examples/**/sandbox[0-9][0-9][0-9]/
examples/**/sandbox_[0-9][0-9][0-9]/

# Everything building_your_first_tool.ipynb generates as it runs: the toy
# event database and external package, and the toolkit the notebook builds
# in Section 5. All of it is reproduced by re-running the notebook.
examples/primer/sandbox/
examples/primer/cms_dimuon/

# The agent script `tb connect orchestral` writes, and the scratch dir it
# works in. Regenerate with `tb connect orchestral` rather than committing;
# the checked-in demos under examples/ are the reference wiring.
.toolbase/agent.py
/sandbox/

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.bbl
*.blg

# Local Claude Code settings (per-clone, not part of toolkit config)
.claude/

# Agent wiring written by `tb connect` — per-clone, and it names the toolbase
# binary in YOUR environment, so it does not transfer between machines. Every
# user runs `tb connect` themselves (see the README). What the agent is served
# is shared through .toolbase/profiles/, which holds no paths.
/.mcp.json
/opencode.json
/.codex/

# INSPIRE query cache (local, regenerated on demand).
.inspire_cache.json

# Background-job scratch (spec/status/log/result per job) — runtime state,
# written under whatever base_directory the jobs bundle runs with.
.jobs/

# Sandbox the lagrangian-extraction example writes into.
examples/lagrangian_extraction/sandbox/

# Stray tool byproducts written to the repo root when a tool runs with
# base_directory=. (audit ledgers, ad-hoc generated models). Not artifacts.
/model/
/audit.json
/audit.md
/*_audit.json
/*_audit.md

# ... but test fixtures under a tool's test_files/ are inputs, not output.
# Without this, committing one needs `git add -f` and is silently skipped
# otherwise (tools/validate/test_validate.py reads a checks-log fixture).
!tools/**/test_files/**/*.log
